CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "e6acf649-b95a-42ad-a464-eae802554253",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-21T03:15:34Z",
  "ticket_id": "0b7c-d811",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "A corpus directory at plugins/dso/data/ui-reference/ with domain-partitioned Markdown files (each \u2264500 lines), YAML frontmatter per entry (id, title, domain[], component[], action[], compliance[], severity, story_type[], coverage, source, license), and three Markdown resolution tiers per entry (### Summary, ### Detail, ### Implementation). A _schema.yaml + check-corpus-schema.sh pre-commit hook enforce tag vocabulary across six dimensions: domain, component, action, compliance, severity, story_type.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system structure with enforced properties (schema validation, file organization, frontmatter requirements) that persists after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "A _index.yaml manifest committed to the repository (not generated at build time), listing every entry with six-dimension tags, one-liner, file path, coverage tier, source, and license. Full inventory readable without loading any corpus file. Regenerated and recommitted on corpus changes.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "uncertain",
        "ranking": 2,
        "rationale": "unclear whether this describes a durable artifact (the manifest exists and is maintained) or a transitional task (creating and committing it), complicated by the regeneration requirement suggesting ongoing maintenance"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "A plugins/dso/scripts/ref-query.sh retrieval script using stdlib Python BM25 (self-contained, no external deps); bm25s used as optional performance accelerator if installed, falls back with stderr notice if not. Flags: --top-n (default 8), --tier=summary|detail|implementation, --session-hash dedup, zero-result stderr signal ([ref-query: no results for query: \"...\" with filters: ...]), completes within 10 seconds.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system capabilities and behaviors (script existence, BM25 implementation, fallback mechanism, flags, performance characteristics) that persist after completion"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Initial corpus covers the full set identified during research: government anti-patterns (all 48 from 17de-a47a at Detail tier; Implementation stretch), USWDS component and token guidance, WCAG 2.2 AAA patterns cross-referenced to Section 508/OMB M-24-08, Nielsen's 10 usability heuristics, Don Norman's principles, GOV.UK Government Design Principles, 18F UX Guide principles, digital.gov federal requirements, Inclusive Design Principles, cognitive load and defensive design checklists, Brignull dark pattern taxonomy, SageSELab AidUI 27-class taxonomy, and representative entries from benbrignell/principles.design. Summary + Detail required for all entries; Implementation is stretch.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable property of the corpus (what it contains and covers) that will remain true once established"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Integration test at tests/integration/test-ref-library.sh (REPO_ROOT-based paths): (a) session-timeout query returns entry tagged auth/forms or containing \"session timeout\" in Summary; (b) --tier=summary output has ### Summary, no ### Implementation; (c) manifest integrity \u2014 every _index.yaml entry resolves to a file at its declared path; (d) no corpus file exceeds 500 lines; (e) precision sub-test \u2014 three representative queries (\"USWDS form validation\", \"WCAG 2.2 keyboard navigation\", \"government authentication anti-pattern\") each return a top result whose frontmatter tags match a predefined expected-tag mapping; (f) completes within 10 seconds.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behaviors that an integration test will continuously verify, phrased as ongoing properties the system should maintain"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "ref-query.sh registered as dso ref-query shim; check-shim-refs.sh does not block downstream skill file references.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system properties of how two components interact and behave together after the work is complete"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "A docs/ui-reference-sources.yaml file at the project root tracks each external reference source: name, URL, type (github-repo|web-spec|website), pinned version/commit, last-synced date, license, and which corpus domains it populates. This is the provenance record for all corpus entries.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system artifact and its ongoing role as a provenance record, not a one-time completion task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    }
  ]
}

